---
// Our Story (About). Built from the shared system, in the homepage's design
// direction. Copy from reference/kodamas-about-page.png, word for word.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import NameHero from '../components/organisms/NameHero.astro';
import CallToActionSection from '../components/organisms/CallToActionSection.astro';
import Section from '../components/molecules/Section.astro';
import Profile from '../components/molecules/Profile.astro';
import Principle from '../components/molecules/Principle.astro';
import Heading from '../components/atoms/Heading.astro';
import Highlight from '../components/atoms/Highlight.astro';
import Button from '../components/atoms/Button.astro';
import { links } from '../data/links';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Our Story · Kodamas"
	description="These meanings mirror Daniela’s Italian heritage and Emma’s expat experience in Japan."
>
	<NameHero
		title="Our Story"
		terms={[
			{ word: 'Ko', meaning: '“co” meaning together' },
			{ word: 'Dama', meaning: '“lady” in Italian' },
		]}
		word="Kodama"
		final="s"
		wisps
	>
		<Fragment slot="meaning">in Japanese, the <Highlight>spirit of the tree</Highlight></Fragment>
		<Fragment slot="note">+ an “S”, because we are two : )</Fragment>
		These meanings mirror <Highlight>Daniela’s Italian heritage</Highlight> and <Highlight
			>Emma’s expat experience in Japan</Highlight
		>. Interestingly, “ko” is also an essential rule in the game of “Go”, preventing the immediate recapture of a stone to
		avoid infinite repetition - something that we find fundamental to continued progress, learning and growth.
	</NameHero>

	<Section labelledby="founders-title" num="01">
		<h2 id="founders-title" class="visually-hidden">Our team</h2>
		<div class="founders">
			<Profile
				name="Emma"
				fullName="Emma Cebuliak"
				zone="Asia/Tokyo"
				link={{ label: 'Visit LinkedIn Profile', href: links.emmaLinkedIn }}
			>
				<Fragment slot="quote">Business requires empathy; it’s <em>the most underrated and unseen skill</em></Fragment>
				<p>
					From the Canadian Rocky Mountains 🏔️ 12 years in Japan.<br />
					Director of Business Growth at <a href={links.happyCowEmma}>HappyCow</a> (6+ years).
				</p>
				<ul slot="more">
					<li>
						Scaled the <a href={links.happyCowPartnerProgram}>Partner Program</a> by 450% to profitability in 18 months.
					</li>
					<li>Lead a team of 20 through acquisition and change management.</li>
					<li>Grew the Instagram community by 110k+.</li>
					<li>Psychology grad.</li>
					<li>Obsessively organized. Found sitting on a bicycle or on the floor.</li>
					<li>
						Wanted to work with Daniela because she’s consistent, reliable, and produced some of the best UX she’d ever
						seen.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</Profile>
			<Profile
				name="Dani"
				fullName="Daniela Contessa"
				zone="Europe/Rome"
				link={{ label: 'Visit LinkedIn Profile', href: links.danielaLinkedIn }}
				reverse
			>
				<Fragment slot="quote">How your team works internally <em>always reflects on your end users.</em></Fragment>
				<p>
					From some of the biggest cities in the world to the countryside growing her own vegetables 🥕🥦🧅. Fractional
					Head of Product, Delivery Manager &amp; Design Lead, at <a href={links.happyCowDaniela}>HappyCow</a> and <a
						href={links.workForImpactDaniela}>Work for Impact</a
					>.
				</p>
				<ul slot="more">
					<li>Built-from-scratch Product Information Management App at <a href={links.wardaDaniela}>WARDA</a></li>
					<li>Loves implementing incident &amp; bug reporting flows.</li>
					<li>Visual Arts and International Relations grad.</li>
					<li>
						Trying to emulate Emma’s bio as she is not great at English copywriting (while doing attempt No.1 of her first
						book, in Italian 🇮🇹).
					</li>
					<li>Wanted to work with Emma because simply seeing her in action was enough to decide to do something good together.</li>
				</ul>
			</Profile>
		</div>
	</Section>

	<Section labelledby="manifesto-title" num="02">
		<Heading level={2} size="statement" id="manifesto-title" reveal>Our <em>Manifesto</em></Heading>
		<div class="manifesto">
			<Principle>
				<Fragment slot="title">People + process = consistent delivery</Fragment>
				<Fragment slot="left">
					<p>
						Companies that have a purpose shouldn’t be thinking only about the mission of the company, they should also be
						concerned about the well-being of their people and culture - first and foremost.
					</p>
					<p>
						Better workflows, less stress, clear and structured patterns for work - these generate more calm and focus,
						and ultimately help your people to truly fulfil your mission - not merely generate higher productivity at a
						high cost.
					</p>
				</Fragment>
				<Fragment slot="right">
					<p>
						<Highlight variant="pink">We don’t buy into the belief that the ends justify the means;</Highlight> we know
						that the product reflects how it’s built.
					</p>
					<p>
						Particularly in our current epoch, the narrative is reflected by “How can AI help me make more money by
						cutting the number of people who work for me?” That viewpoint contains a big fallacy, because it sets up
						productivity to defy the very people it’s supposed to support in the first place.
					</p>
				</Fragment>
			</Principle>
			<Principle>
				<Fragment slot="title">
					AI should help you be more successful by making your people more successful. More, not less.
				</Fragment>
				<Fragment slot="left">
					<p>
						Therefore, we are all for helping companies that want to incorporate technology (including AI) thoroughly, but
						in an ethical way.
					</p>
					<ul>
						<li>We are not going to help you reduce your team with AI.</li>
						<li>
							If you’re looking for someone to cut your costs by reducing the number of people on your team, you should
							leave this page now.
						</li>
						<li>The mark of a good company is being able to support people, not to get rid of them.</li>
					</ul>
				</Fragment>
				<Fragment slot="right">
					<p><Highlight variant="pink">Delivery isn’t about control; it’s about clarity.</Highlight></p>
					<p>
						We build lean, empathetic frameworks that help ambitious teams focus on what matters, anticipate what’s next,
						and ship with confidence - in a way that empowers, not diminish.
					</p>
					<Button href={links.blogfolio}>Read Our Blogfolio 📝</Button>
				</Fragment>
			</Principle>
		</div>
	</Section>

	<div class="cta-gap">
		<CallToActionSection
			num="03"
			title="Want to optimize your internal workflows?"
			cta={{ label: 'Connect With Us', href: links.connect }}
		>
			<p>
				At <strong>Kodamas</strong>, we help teams design scalable systems that reduce friction, improve communication, and
				make collaboration effortless.
			</p>
			<p>If your bug reporting or internal ops feel like chaos, let’s turn them into clarity.</p>
		</CallToActionSection>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.founders {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: var(--layout-section);
	}
	.manifesto {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: var(--space-10);
		margin-top: var(--space-8);
	}
	/* The bright section follows a navy one: keep the one section gap above it */
	.cta-gap {
		margin-top: var(--layout-section);
	}
</style>
